{
  "id": "deck-item-put-remove",
  "title": "Concurrent adds and removes in a user deck",
  "covers": [
    "deck_item: identity is (deck_id, item_key); whole-row last-writer-wins; removal is reversible"
  ],
  "narrative": [
    "B syncs first, then A.",
    "食べる: A adds (T+10), B removes (T+20), A adds again (T+30): present, at A's last position. (B's remove reached the server before A's first put; the tombstone it created made that older put lose.)",
    "持つ: both add it offline (B at T+11, A at T+12): one row; A's later position wins.",
    "待つ: B removes an item (T+13) the server has never seen: a tombstone row is created so that A's OLDER put (T+5), which arrives afterwards, loses.",
    "A removed row is canonical (position 0, occurrence_count 0, added_at = deleted_at = wall time of the remove), so replicas agree on it whatever they held before."
  ],
  "devices": {
    "A": "01931f3e-0000-7000-8000-0000000000a1",
    "B": "01931f3e-0000-7000-8000-0000000000b2",
    "S": "00000000-0000-7000-8000-000000000001"
  },
